## 🟡 Step 2 – Better but Without Dummy Node
Instead of creating new nodes, just **relink** existing nodes.

👉 Idea:
- Pick the smaller head as the start (`head`).  
- Move `tail` pointer forward, attaching nodes as you go.  

### Code
```c
struct ListNode* mergeTwoLists(struct ListNode* l1, struct ListNode* l2) {
    if (l1 == NULL) return l2;
    if (l2 == NULL) return l1;

    struct ListNode* head;
    if (l1->val < l2->val) {
        head = l1;
        l1 = l1->next;
    } else {
        head = l2;
        l2 = l2->next;
    }

    struct ListNode* tail = head;

    while (l1 != NULL && l2 != NULL) {
        if (l1->val < l2->val) {
            tail->next = l1;
            l1 = l1->next;
        } else {
            tail->next = l2;
            l2 = l2->next;
        }
        tail = tail->next;
    }

    // Attach remaining
    if (l1 != NULL) tail->next = l1;
    if (l2 != NULL) tail->next = l2;

    return head;
}
```

👉 This is much cleaner — **no extra memory**, just pointer rewiring.  

