# 🥈 Problem 2: Palindrome Linked List (#234)

### 🔑 Problem
Check if linked list reads the same forward & backward.  

---

### 🔴 Brute Force (Easy to Think)
- Copy list into an array.  
- Use two-pointer check (start, end).  

👉 Works, but uses **O(n) extra space**.  

---

### 🟢 Optimized Approach (O(1) Space)
- Use **slow & fast pointers** to reach the middle.  
- Reverse the second half.  
- Compare first half & reversed second half.  
- (Optional) Reverse second half again to restore list.  

---

### ✅ Code
```c
bool isPalindrome(struct ListNode* head) {
    if (head == NULL || head->next == NULL) return true;

    // Step 1: Find middle (slow/fast)
    struct ListNode* slow = head;
    struct ListNode* fast = head;
    while (fast->next != NULL && fast->next->next != NULL) {
        slow = slow->next;
        fast = fast->next->next;
    }

    // Step 2: Reverse second half
    struct ListNode* prev = NULL;
    struct ListNode* curr = slow->next;
    while (curr != NULL) {
        struct ListNode* next = curr->next;
        curr->next = prev;
        prev = curr;
        curr = next;
    }

    // Step 3: Compare halves
    struct ListNode* p1 = head;
    struct ListNode* p2 = prev;
    bool result = true;
    while (p2 != NULL) {
        if (p1->val != p2->val) {
            result = false;
            break;
        }
        p1 = p1->next;
        p2 = p2->next;
    }

    return result;
}
```

